    "title": "Forney's Avery Pitts tosses shutout gem in Game 1 win over Denton Guyer in state semifinals - NewsBreak",
    "text": "By Rick Kretzschmar ,\n1 days ago ALLEN — A little change in time and temperature meant little to Avery Pitts on Tuesday. The sophomore pitcher from Forney was locked in. Pitts tossed a one-hit shutout while striking out 14 batters as Forney edged Denton Guyer 1-0 in Game 1 of a best-of-three Class 6A Division II state semifinal series at the Allen High School softball field. Pitts (19-1) combined riseballs with movement with corner-biting curveballs to keep Guyer guessing. Guyer’s lone hit was a single to center by Lexi Wrice with two outs in the bottom of the fifth inning. Pitts had one walk, to Annaleeia Martinez in the second inning. Read full article\nRead in NewsBreak",
    "summary": "1 days ago ALLEN — A little change in time and temperature meant little to Avery Pitts on Tuesday. Pitts tossed a one-hit shutout while striking out 14 batters as Forney edged Denton Guyer 1-0 in Game 1 of a best-of-three Class 6A Division II state semifinal series at the Allen High School softball field. Pitts (19-1) combined riseballs with movement with corner-biting curveballs to keep Guyer guessing. Guyer’s lone hit was a single to center by Lexi Wrice with two outs in the bottom of the fifth inning. Pitts had one walk, to Annaleeia Martinez in the second inning.",
